{title: 040 - The Dawn of God's Dear Sabbath}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #040 • ST. GEORGES BOLTON • 7.6.7.6.8.6.7.7}
{lyricist: Ada Cross}
{composer: J. Walch}
{key: Db}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 40}
{meta: tune ST. GEORGES BOLTON}
{meta: meter 7.6.7.6.8.6.7.7}
{meta: category Worship - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Db]The [Fm/Ab]dawn [Ab7]of God's dear [Db]Sabbath
[Db]Breaks [Gb]o'er the earth again,
[Db]As [Fm/Ab]some [Ab7]sweet summer [Ebm/Bb]morning
[Bbm/Db]After [Fm]a [Db]night [Ebm]of [Ab]pain;
[Ab]It comes [Ab7/Gb]as [Gb]cooling [Db/F]showers
[Db]To [Bbm]some exhausted [Ebm]land,
[Ebm]As [Fm]shade [Db]of clustered [Gb]palm [Ab7/Gb]trees
[Gdim]'Mid weary [Db/Ab]wastes [Ab7]of [Db]sand.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Db]Lord, we [Fm/Ab]would [Ab7]bring for offering,
[Db]Though [Gb]marred with earthly [Db]soil,
[Db]A [Fm/Ab]week [Ab7]of earnest [Ebm/Bb]labor,
[Bbm/Db]Of [Ab/C]steady, [Db]faithful [Ab]toil,
[Ab]Fair [Ab7/Gb]fruits of [Gb]self [Ab7/Gb]denial,
[Db]Of [Bbm]strong, deep [Gb]love [Bbm]to [Ebm]Thee,
[Ebm]Fostered [Db]by Thine own [Gb]Spirit,
[Gdim]In [Db/Ab]true humility.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Db]And [Fm/Ab]we [Ab7]would bring our [Db]burden
[Db]Of [Gb]sinful thought and [Db]deed,
[Db]In [Fm/Ab]Thy [Ab7]pure presence [Ebm/Bb]kneeling,
[Bbm/Db]From [Ab/C]bondage [Db]to [Ebm]be [Ab]freed,
[Ab]Our [Ab7/Gb]heart's most [Gb]bitter [Db/F]sorrow
[Db]For [Bbm]all Thy [Gb]work [Bbm]undone-
[Ebm]So [Fm]many [Db]talents [Gb]wasted!
[Gdim]So [Db/Ab]few bright [Ab7]laurels [Db]won!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Db]And [Fm/Ab]with [Ab7]that sorrow [Db]mingling,
[Db]A [Gb]steadfast faith, and [Db]sure,
[Db]And [Fm/Ab]love [Ab7]so deep and [Ebm/Bb]fervent,
[Bbm/Db]For [Ab/C]Thee [Fm]to [Db]make [Ebm]it [Ab]pure,
[Ab]In [Ab7/Gb]Thy dear [Gb]presence [Db/F]finding
[Db]The [Bbm]pardon [Gb]that [Bbm]we [Ebm]need,
[Ebm]And [Fm]then [Db]the peace so [Gb]lasting-
[Gdim]Celestial [Ab7]peace indeed.
{end_of_verse}
